+      // whose duration depends on how far the tab is and how fast the
+      // device is. A single fixed-delay measurement (previously 50ms) goes
+      // stale mid-scroll, which is exactly why the indicator landed in the
+      // wrong spot for tabs further along the row — Journal, Mentees,
+      // Requests, Settings — after scrolling past Support. Instead, keep
+      // re-measuring on every animation frame for a bit after any
+      // navigation or scroll, so the indicator always lands on the tab's
+      // final resting position.
+      let navSyncRAF = null;
